# Dungeon Run

C++20 / SDL3 top-down multiplayer dungeon game. Design docs in `docs/` — read `docs/ROADMAP.md` for current phase.

## Stack & architecture

- Local play first; listen-server P2P later. Reusable `net/` must not include SDL.
- Fixed timestep sim in `src/game/`; SDL lifecycle/loop in `src/app/`; draw-only in `src/render/`.
- `game` never calls SDL render APIs; `render` never mutates gameplay state.
- Prefer simple structs/arrays until complexity forces ECS.

## Workflow with Dragostin

- He often implements game logic himself in Ask mode — coach and review; do not take over coding unless he asks or switches to Agent for implementation.
- When finishing a milestone together, update `docs/ROADMAP.md` (checkboxes + progress log).
- Keep changes scoped; no drive-by refactors or unsolicited markdown beyond docs he wants updated.

## Build (Windows)

```powershell
cmake --build build
.\build\dungeon_run.exe
```

New terminals may need PATH refresh if `cmake`/`g++` are missing after install.
